One way to return errors in C is by using return codes. This involves assigning a specific value to the return type of a function to indicate an error.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

// Function to check if a file exists
int check_file_exists(const char *filename) {
    // Simulate a file operation
    if (/* file operation fails */) {
        return -1; // Return an error code
    }
